The '''God capes''' are a set of [[magic]] [[capes]] awarded from the [[Mage Arena I]] [[miniquest]]. After defeating [[Kolodion]], the player can speak to him and step through the [[sparkling pool]] to a cave where they can pray to one of three [[gods]]: [[Saradomin]], [[Zamorak]], or [[Guthix]]. After praying to a god, the corresponding cape will appear at the statue's feet and may be picked up. After claiming their first cape, players can talk to the [[Chamber guardian]] to claim the corresponding [[god staves|god staff]]. Multiple capes from the same statue can be obtained.

If lost, a player can get a new cape by once again praying at the statue without needing to fight Kolodion again. It may be a good idea to get multiple copies of the same cape. Alternatively, players can purchase any one of the three capes from [[Perdu]] for {{coins|23,000}}.

God capes offer the second highest Magic Attack bonus of any cape, outclassed only by their imbued variants and require a Magic level of 60 to wear. All god capes have the same stats, with the only differences between them being [[God Wars Dungeon]] alignment and corresponding [[god spell]]. 

